INT. HOLLOWAY & DRAKE, OPEN-PLAN FLOOR, "SYNERGY POD" - DAY

A glass cube in the middle of forty identical desks. Beanbags. A whiteboard reading "WINS!!" in six colors. A mini-fridge hums with kombucha.

BRENT STOLLER, thirties, vest over a Henley, paces in front of the board holding a ceremonial marker. DEIRDRE KOH, forties, brisk, with a pen behind each ear, sits cross-legged on a beanbag. QUINCY ABARA, twenties, the junior analyst, perches on the edge of a stool, holding a laptop like a shield.

                    BRENT
          Team, great energy. I just want to say, we are crushing Q3.

                    DEIRDRE
          We missed Q3.

                    BRENT
          We pre-crushed it. In spirit.

Quincy scribbles. Deirdre catches her eye and mouths something. She mouths it back. Neither smiles.

                    QUINCY
          Brent, should I put "pre-crushed" in the deck?

                    BRENT
          Absolutely. Bold it.

She does. The fridge hums. Everything seems fine.

The glass door slides open. AUGUSTINE VANCE-PELL, sixty, chief executive, silver and enormous in a camel coat, enters with a binder under one arm and a wide, serene smile.

Brent's marker stops moving. Deirdre rises from the beanbag in one smooth motion, like someone leaving a bomb site. Quincy shuts her laptop.

                    AUGUSTINE
          Please. Don't stop on my account.

He walks to the whiteboard and reads it, lips moving. Then he turns, and the smile has not changed at all.

                    AUGUSTINE (CONT'D)
          I have a very short announcement. Who would like to hear it?

Nobody speaks. Deirdre raises her hand, as if at school.
